      "better_line": "Untap a black-producing land like Watery Grave, Breeding Pool, or Wastewood Verge to gain extra mana for casting additional spells from hand this turn (e.g., Formidable Speaker for 3 mana, or work toward casting Overlord of the Balemurk or Deceit)",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 136,
      "player": "GPT4om Stoic",
      "decision_index": 95,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Selected Harvester of Misery (which is in the graveyard) as a target permanent. If this is Formidable Speaker's untap ability or another effect targeting battlefield permanents, this choice seems invalid or suboptimal. A land or the Overlord of the Balemurk would be more useful targets to untap.",
      "action_taken": "Targeted Harvester of Misery (in graveyard) for a permanent-targeting effect",
      "better_line": "Target a meaningful battlefield permanent like Overlord of the Balemurk or a tapped land to gain additional mana or utility",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 136,
      "player": "GPT4om Stoic",
      "decision_index": 95,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Discarded Deceit instead of the redundant second copy of Ardyn, the Usurper. Deceit has an evoke cost of just {U/B}{U/B} (2 mana), providing cheap interaction (bounce a permanent or force a discard) which is valuable when most lands are tapped. The second Ardyn is legendary and redundant - only one can be on the battlefield at a time.",
      "action_taken": "Discarded Deceit to Formidable Speaker's tutor ability",
      "better_line": "Discard the second Ardyn, the Usurper (legendary duplicate) and keep Deceit for its cheap evoke interaction against an opponent who likely has countermagic and board control",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 138,
      "player": "GPT4om Stoic",
      "decision_index": 97,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Get Lost is targeting Harvester of Misery, but Harvester of Misery is in the opponent's graveyard, not on the battlefield. Looking at the opponent's battlefield, the threats are Overlord of the Balemurk (tapped), two Formidable Speakers (tapped), and lands. At 3 life, the critical threat is Overlord of the Balemurk which will become a 5/5 creature soon (it had 5 impending counters, 2 were removed in prior turns, so it likely has 0-1 counters left and is already a creature given it's listed without impending notation). Day of Judgment would clear all three creatures at once and is available. Using Get Lost on a single creature while Day of Judgment is available and would handle all threats is a significant waste of resources, especially at 3 life where the opponent giving you two Map tokens is irrelevant compared to clearing the whole board.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Get Lost targeting a single creature (reportedly Harvester of Misery, which appears to be an invalid or confused target)",
      "better_line": "Cast Day of Judgment to destroy all three opposing creatures (Overlord of the Balemurk and two Formidable Speakers) at once, then hold up countermagic like No More Lies or Spell Snare for the opponent's next play.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 150,
      "player": "KimiK2 Spike",
      "decision_index": 103,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "GPT4om Stoic has lethal on board with two Formidable Speakers (2+2=4 damage) against an opponent at 3 life with no blockers. Casting Overlord of the Balemurk precombat is unnecessary and gives the opponent additional information and interaction windows before the lethal attack.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Overlord of the Balemurk in precombat main phase before attacking for lethal.",
      "better_line": "Go directly to combat and attack with both Formidable Speakers for 4 damage, killing the opponent at 3 life. Cast spells only if needed post-combat.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 153,
      "player": "GPT4om Stoic",
      "decision_index": 105,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Opponent is at 3 life with no creatures. Two Formidable Speakers (2/4 each) can attack for 4 total damage, which is lethal. Activating Formidable Speaker's {1}, {T} untap ability taps one of them, reducing the attack to only 2 damage and missing lethal.",
      "action_taken": "Activated Formidable Speaker's tap ability to untap a permanent, tapping one of the two attackers needed for lethal.",
      "better_line": "Pass priority without activating anything, then attack with both Formidable Speakers for 4 damage to kill the opponent at 3 life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 154,
      "player": "GPT4om Stoic",
      "decision_index": 112,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Tapped Formidable Speaker to untap Overlord of the Balemurk which was likely already untapped, unnecessarily reducing the number of attackers. While the remaining attackers (5+2=7) are still lethal against opponent at 3 life, this is wasteful and could matter if opponent has interaction to remove one attacker.",
      "action_taken": "Used Formidable Speaker's tap ability to untap Overlord of the Balemurk",
      "better_line": "Keep both Formidable Speakers untapped to attack with all creatures (5+2+2=9 damage), maximizing overkill to play around potential removal or tricks from the opponent at 3 life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 154,
      "player": "GPT4om Stoic",
      "decision_index": 112,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Casting Harvester of Misery before combat gives all other creatures -2/-2, shrinking the two Formidable Speakers to 0/2 and Overlord to 3/3. While still likely lethal with Harvester's 5 power (menace) + Overlord's 3 = 8 vs 3 life, this is unnecessarily risky compared to just attacking with the existing board of 9 power (5+2+2) into an opponent at 3 life with no blockers. The -2/-2 makes the Speakers unable to deal any damage and could matter if the opponent has removal for one attacker.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Harvester of Misery before combat, giving own creatures -2/-2",
      "better_line": "Skip to combat and attack with Overlord of the Balemurk (5/5) and both Formidable Speakers (2/4 each) for 9 damage against 3 life - guaranteed lethal regardless of Restless Anchorage blocking",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 168,
      "player": "GPT4om Stoic",
      "decision_index": 123,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "GPT4om Stoic used Formidable Speaker's untap ability ({1}, {T}: Untap another target permanent) but targeted Meticulous Archive, an opponent's land. This gives the opponent a free untap on one of their lands, providing them with additional mana or options. The ability should be used to untap one of their own permanents for value, or not used at all. With Harvester of Misery on the stack (which gives other creatures -2/-2 on ETB), untapping their own Formidable Speaker or a land would have been far more useful. Untapping an opponent's land is actively harmful.",
      "action_taken": "Used Formidable Speaker's untap ability targeting opponent's Meticulous Archive, giving the opponent a free untapped land.",
      "better_line": "Target one of their own permanents (like their other Formidable Speaker, Overlord of the Balemurk, or a tapped land) to gain value, or simply not activate the ability if no beneficial target exists.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 168,
      "player": "GPT4om Stoic",
      "decision_index": 123,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Tapping a Formidable Speaker to untap the other Formidable Speaker accomplishes nothing useful while removing a potential attacker. With the opponent at 3 life and no blockers, every point of damage matters. Even though Harvester's -2/-2 would reduce Speakers to 0/2 power, having both untapped for combat is still better than needlessly tapping one.",
      "action_taken": "Activated Formidable Speaker's untap ability targeting the other Formidable Speaker, tapping one for no net benefit.",
      "better_line": "Don't activate the ability. Keep both Formidable Speakers untapped for combat. Attack with Harvester of Misery (5/4 with menace) and both Speakers for lethal damage against the opponent at 3 life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 168,
      "player": "GPT4om Stoic",
      "decision_index": 123,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "GPT4om Stoic chose to untap the opponent's Hallowed Fountain instead of one of their own lands. Untapping an opponent's land gives them additional mana while providing no benefit, whereas untapping their own land (like Watery Grave or Breeding Pool) would give them additional mana to work with.",
      "action_taken": "Selected opponent's Hallowed Fountain as the target to untap",
